{"text":"MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "The Brass Bottle felt like a natural next choice because its magical comedy premise connects with what appealed to me about HOCUS POCUS.",
    "That choice fits my current interest in something light and funny, rather than simply another film."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "The Tomorrow War missed my mood because science fiction action does not offer the light comedy I want right now.",
    "I could not establish whether the unidentified films matched my interests, so I would skip them rather than assume I would enjoy them."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "The choices seem to treat interest in one film as a reason to watch other films without enough connection to their tone.",
    "An unusual premise alone is not enough for me; magical comedy and science fiction action appeal to different moods."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "The playful combination of magic and humor matters more to me right now than a broad connection to imaginative stories.",
    "Because I rarely interact, I need a clear reason to expect that a film will suit my mood before choosing it."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The Brass Bottle captured my interest in light magical comedy, but the other choices gave me little reason to expect the same enjoyment."
}"}
